# Pre-commit intentionally does NOT lint or typecheck.
#
# lint-staged fanned eslint out over parallel chunks and the hook also ran a
# full `tsc --noEmit`; on a loaded machine that was enough to get the chunks
# OOM-killed mid-commit, leaving a stale .git/index.lock behind.
#
# Verification now happens ONCE: the full gate suite is run in the foreground
# before pushing a batch, and authoritatively in CI. Commits stay cheap so work
# can be checkpointed often (see the incremental-commit rule) instead of being
# held hostage to a multi-minute hook. This hook is a deliberate no-op.
exit 0
